  {
    "episode_id": 72778,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72778.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "I know I'm going to be stopping by and addressing the rural caucus at the Democratic Party and I hope that from an agriculture standpoint that will have some discussion of some of the rural issues. I think that's important. I think basically people want to see a vision and a positive vision. There's a lot of negativity at the Republican Convention, and I'm sure the Democratic one, there'll be some too, but I'm hopeful that we'll be able to hear a positive vision going forward, because that's what I hear from people. They want to figure out how they're going to get access to broadband, the opiate crisis, which has hit every rural",
