        "text": "Economic development and public safety in agriculture depend on advanced digital infrastructure.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Rural communities deserve equitable technological infrastructure similar to urban centers.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Existing federal programs like the Universal Service Fund are capable of being redirected effectively toward broadband deployment.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Public policy change can be driven successfully through bipartisan legislative coordination.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Investing in rural broadband will yield measurable improvements in productivity, resilience, and quality of life.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The current state of rural internet access undermines preparedness for future public health emergencies.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Audiences value fairness and equity in national infrastructure investment decisions.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Federal funding mechanisms can be adapted creatively without requiring new legislation.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "Senator Soon holds sufficient influence within the Senate Commerce Committee to catalyze meaningful action.",
