    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, they've used some rule-making ways to do this. And have been, I'm sure, whether there's lawsuits or not, I don't know. But they did have some leeway under the statute, depending on what they could find names they could make, which would support them making these changes. And so that's why we push back and said you're wrong with the reasons you've used, because we think What you're doing is going to severely impact the development of advanced file fuels. And so that's why we have some pretty liberal senators who are not from big ag states on our side, because they said along with conservative Republicans who cares about this in our state, they said, this isn't right. You're going to actually stop the development of these new advanced file fuels that are better environmentally, certainly better than oil. And so we had some good arguments. We keep pushing back at them that they're going to chill investments and other things. You know, I was glad they made some improvements and we'd like to see even more.",
